spoint gh-pages WorkerEntry bundling (scripts/bundle-worker.mjs + esbuild devDep): the bundle step MUST run BEFORE the gh-pages.yml 'Patch paths' step, not after. The patch step seds /src/ -> /spoint/src/ and /node_modules/ -> /spoint/node_modules/ across all dist JS; if you bundle after, WorkerEntry's SDK imports are already absolute /spoint/src/... and the external rule excludes them so esbuild inlines NOTHING (deployed WorkerEntry.js came out 2599 bytes, a silent no-op that still works but gives zero bundling benefit). Bundle BEFORE patch when imports are still relative -> esbuild resolves+inlines the SDK graph (356KB). The plugin keeps external only runtime-fetched deps (jolt browser wasm.js + node wasm-compat, /node_modules importmap-bypass xstate/d3-octree/msgpackr, node:*/draco3dgltf which are process.versions?.node-dead). Rewrite bare importmap-bypass deps to absolute /node_modules/... (BASE='') so the generic patch sed then prefixes /spoint - do NOT emit /spoint directly or the sed double-prefixes to /spoint/spoint/. Witness the bundle by spawning it as a real `new Worker(url,{type:module})` and asserting WORKER_READY (browser-39) - a clean build is NOT proof it inlined; CHECK THE DEPLOYED SIZE (HEAD content-length) - 2599 bytes = no-op, ~356KB+ = inlined. BrowserServer still loads src/sdk/WorkerEntry.js (on deploy = the bundle, no client change). Commit f71d7e18 fixed the ordering after b284faee shipped the no-op.